Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-24-2001||12:21 AM||||Yeah, begin looking for another car! J/K...man you've got me stumped on that one...anybody?............<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||5
Z||000002||fierogtracer||09-24-2001||12:41 AM||||There is a relay under the dash on the right side of the steering wheel it is mounted to a heatsink. that is exactly what it is.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_11.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||09-24-2001||01:00 AM||||yup, I've had the same problem.  However, I left mine for about a year before I did anything about it.  There could actually be two things:  The relay under the dash.  (It's above the accelerator, and nothing has to be removed to get at it.)  Or else the rheostat (the dimmer dial on the dash panel).  Personally, I replaced both.  However my problem was that they'd go, come back, and go again.  I figured that was from the dimmer, but the last time they went, they were gone, so that had to have been the relay.  I'd replace the relay first.  (cost me about $50CDN for a brand new one)  Then if you're still having problems, get the rheostat.  Best of luck!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
